Preamble (non-binding statement of intent)

  This license is intended to make Blackbox available for personal,
  educational, academic research, non-commercial research, nonprofit use,
  internal productivity / automation / research / evaluation (including by
  for-profit organizations), and non-commercial modification and
  redistribution, while preserving copyright and attribution, restricting
  commercial offerings where Blackbox is a Material Component, and
  reserving a separate commercial-license path to the project owner. The
  preamble is descriptive; it is not itself a grant or a prohibition.


SECTION 1. DEFINITIONS

  1.1 "Software" means the Blackbox software, in source and binary form,
      made available under this license.

  1.2 "Commercial Use" means use of the Software, in whole or in part,
      in connection with any of:

        (a) Sale / sublicensing - selling, reselling, or sublicensing the
            Software or any Derivative Work, or selling access to it, for
            monetary or other material consideration;

        (b) Paid SaaS / hosted service - operating the Software (or a
            Derivative Work, or functionality substantially provided by the
            Software) as a service that third parties access for a fee,
            where the Software is a Material Component of what is offered;

        (c) Paid consulting / paid service - charging third parties for
            consulting, integration, customization, training, or support
            where the Software is a Material Component of what is offered;

        (d) Commercial product integration - bundling or incorporating the
            Software or a Derivative Work into a commercial product, or
            using them internally as a Material Component of a commercial
            product or service.

      "Commercial Use" does NOT include Internal Use (Section 1.7) where
      the Software is not a Material Component of any paid offering, and
      does NOT include personal side work where the Software is incidental.

  1.3 "Non-Commercial Use" means use of the Software for purposes that
      are not Commercial Use, including without limitation personal use,
      education, academic research, non-commercial research, nonprofit use,
      government / public-sector use in non-revenue contexts, and Internal
      Use by any party - including for-profit - where the Software is not
      a Material Component of any paid offering.

  1.4 "Distribution" means any act of making copies of the Software or a
      Derivative Work available to a third party, including but not
      limited to uploading to a public code-hosting platform; publishing
      in a software registry; bundling into a larger distribution; sending
      as part of a consultancy deliverable; offering as a downloadable
      artifact; making available on a network-accessible server from which
      third parties can fetch it; and providing it as part of a paid or
      unpaid training program (the latter only if not already classified
      as Commercial Use).

      Internal use within a single Organization by employees and
      contractors acting on its behalf is NOT Distribution; it is Use.

  1.5 "Derivative Work" (also "Modification") means any work that
      incorporates all or a substantial part of the Software, including
      translations, ports, adaptations, or modifications of the source
      code; works that statically or dynamically link to the Software;
      works that bundle the Software as a sub-component; and works that
      expose the Software's functionality through an API such that the
      Software is the primary engine of the combined system.

      Mere aggregation in a collection (e.g. a curated list of unrelated
      tools) does not by itself create a Derivative Work, provided that
      the Software remains an independent work and is distributed with
      this License intact.

  1.6 "Attribution" identifies Blackbox as the source/origin of the
      Software or Derivative Work. It does NOT require making complete
      corresponding source code available. "Attribution" means all of:

        (a) an unmodified copyright notice identifying Blackbox /
            LeiD215 (or successor entity, if any, as recorded in NOTICE)
            as the source;

        (b) the full text of this License;

        (c) a clear statement of any Material Modifications made by the
            distributor (date, scope, and identifier of the modified
            version);

        (d) in the case of a Derivative Work distributed as source, a
            prominent pointer (e.g. a NOTICE file or README section)
            identifying the upstream Blackbox version from which the
            Derivative Work was derived;

        (e) permissible factual naming wording per Section 3.5.

  1.7 "Use" (also "Internal Use" when performed internally) means
      executing the Software, interacting with its outputs, training or
      evaluating on its outputs, and similar activities performed
      internally within an Organization or by an Individual, without
      making the Software, its outputs, or substantially Blackbox-derived
      functionality available to a third party.

  1.8 "Organization" means any legal person other than an Individual,
      including corporations, partnerships, LLCs, non-profits,
      government bodies, academic institutions, and informal collectives
      acting in a coordinated capacity.

      "Individual" means a natural person acting in a personal capacity
      and not on behalf of an Organization.

  1.9 "Material Component" means a component, module, or set of
      capabilities whose absence would materially change the value,
      function, or commercial appeal of the larger product, service, or
      offering. Whether the Software is a Material Component of a paid
      offering is determined by an objective reasonable-person test
      applied to the paid offering as marketed and delivered, not by
      internal-architecture labels alone.

      The Software is NOT a Material Component of:

        - internal productivity / automation / research / evaluation
          tools where the Software is one of many internal dependencies;
        - a paid deliverable where the Software is incidental and a
          reasonable customer would not consider Blackbox to be the
          principal value of what is offered;
        - an internal QA / testing pipeline that runs against other
          software without Blackbox being externally observable to the
          customer.

      The Software IS a Material Component of:

        - a paid hosted service whose headline capability is provided by
          Blackbox;
        - a paid product whose marketing, documentation, or pricing
          depends on Blackbox functionality;
        - a Derivative Work that is itself the principal thing being
          sold or licensed.

  1.10 "Project Owner" means LeiD215 or a successor entity designated in
       the NOTICE file accompanying the Software.

  1.11 "DCO" means the Developer Certificate of Origin version 1.1 (or
       its successor), under which contributors certify their right to
       submit contributions.

  1.12 "Patent Grant". This License does NOT include any operative
       patent grant. No license under any patent is granted, expressly or
       by implication, estoppel, or exhaustion, by this License.


SECTION 2. PERMITTED USES

  Subject to the conditions in Section 3, the following are permitted:

  2.1 Personal use of the Software by an Individual for non-commercial
      purposes.

  2.2 Education: use by Individuals and educational institutions in
      coursework, teaching, training material, and student projects.
      No Commercial Use arises.

  2.3 Research: use for academic research, non-commercial research, and
      personal research, including reproduction of experimental results
      in non-commercial publications, dissertations, and pre-prints.
      No Commercial Use arises.

  2.4 Nonprofit use: use by a registered non-profit organization in
      pursuit of its non-profit mission, provided no paid offering of
      access to the Software results.

  2.5 Internal Use: use by any party - Individual or Organization,
      including for-profit - for productivity, automation, research,
      evaluation, QA, or testing, where the Software is not a Material
      Component of any paid offering.

  2.6 Personal side work: use by an Individual for personal commercial
      side work where the Software is incidental and not a Material
      Component of the paid deliverable or service.

  2.7 Non-commercial modification and Distribution of the Software and
      Derivative Works, subject to the conditions in Section 3.


SECTION 3. CONDITIONS ON PERMITTED USES

  Every Distribution of the Software or a Derivative Work must include,
  in a place reasonably discoverable by each recipient:

  3.1 An unmodified copyright notice identifying the Project Owner as
      the source.

  3.2 The full text of this License (no summaries, no external links in
      place of the text).

  3.3 If the distributed work is a Derivative Work, a clear and dated
      modification marker, identifying the upstream Blackbox version
      from which the Derivative Work was derived.

  3.4 Any NOTICE file present in the upstream distribution, carried
      through unmodified.

  3.5 Permissible factual naming wording. The Distributor MAY use
      "Based on Blackbox" or "Powered by Blackbox" for truthful
      attribution of source. The Distributor MUST NOT use wording that
      implies official endorsement, affiliation, or an "Official
      Blackbox" status without prior written permission from the
      Project Owner.

  NOTE: "Attribution" under this Section means identifying Blackbox as
  the source/origin. It does NOT impose a mandatory obligation to
  disclose, publish, or otherwise make available complete corresponding
  source code of the Software or any Derivative Work, except where such
  obligation arises from a separate written agreement or from
  applicable law independent of this License.


SECTION 4. PROHIBITED USES

  Unless you have obtained a separate written commercial license from
  the Project Owner (Section 7), you MUST NOT:

  4.1 Sell, resell, or sublicense the Software or any Derivative Work,
      or sell access to it, for monetary or other material consideration.

  4.2 Operate the Software (or a Derivative Work, or functionality
      substantially provided by the Software) as a paid SaaS, hosted
      service, paid managed service, paid training, paid consulting,
      paid support, paid integration, or any similar paid offering, in
      any pricing model including subscription, per-call, metered,
      freemium-with-paid-tier, or otherwise, where the Software is a
      Material Component of what is offered.

  4.3 Bundle or incorporate the Software or a Derivative Work into a
      commercial product, or use them internally as a Material Component
      of a commercial product or service.

  4.4 Structure an arrangement that uses Section 5.3 (cloud-cost
      reimbursement) as a pretext to operate a paid hosted service.
      Section 5.3 is narrow; disguised commercial hosting falls under
      Section 4.2.

  4.5 Use the names "Blackbox", "LeiD215", or any contributor name to
      imply endorsement of any product, service, or Derivative Work
      without the Project Owner's prior written consent. Factual
      attribution per Section 3.5 is permitted.


SECTION 5. NON-COMMERCIAL EXCEPTION CLARIFICATIONS

  The following clarifications apply to the definitions in Section 1
  and the prohibitions in Section 4. They are binding to the extent
  they clarify those Sections. They are NOT exhaustive.

  5.1 Donations, sponsorships, and grants accepted by a downstream user
      are NOT Commercial Use, provided the donation/sponsorship/grant
      is not a precondition for receiving the Software and is not paid
      in exchange for access to the Software.

  5.2 Use by a registered non-profit organization in pursuit of its
      non-profit mission is Non-Commercial Use, provided no paid
      offering of access to the Software results.

  5.3 Cloud-cost, infrastructure-cost, or electricity-cost reimbursement
      is not Commercial Use, provided that:

        (a) the reimbursement is limited to documented out-of-pocket
            infrastructure cost;

        (b) the recipient does not profit from the reimbursement;

        (c) there is no commercial service intent (i.e. the
            reimbursement is not a mechanism by which a third party pays
            for access to a hosted Software-as-a-Service);

        (d) the arrangement does not amount to disguised commercial
            hosting.

      This Section 5.3 is narrow; see Section 4.4.

  5.4 Hackathon prizes and similar awards are not Commercial Use with
      respect to the Software; they are compensation for participation,
      not for the Software itself.

  5.5 Government and inter-governmental use in a non-revenue context is
      Non-Commercial Use.

  5.6 Personal side-gig use by an Individual is Commercial Use under
      Section 1.2(c) if the Software is a Material Component of the paid
      deliverable. If the Software is incidental, the use is permitted
      under Section 2.6.

  5.7 Education, academic research, non-commercial research, and
      nonprofit use are permitted under Sections 2.2 / 2.3 / 2.4
      respectively. Nothing in this Section 5 expands Commercial Use.


SECTION 6. CONTRIBUTIONS

  6.1 Every contribution to the Software MUST carry a Signed-off-by
      line, in the form:

        Signed-off-by: Contributor Name <contributor@example.com>

      certifying the contributor's right to submit the contribution
      under the DCO 1.1 text (or its successor).

  6.2 By submitting a contribution, the contributor grants the Project
      Owner a sufficient license to:

        (a) incorporate the contribution into the Software under this
            License;

        (b) relicense the contribution under a separate commercial
            license to a third party under Section 7;

        (c) relicense the contribution under any future version of the
            Blackbox community license.

  6.3 No CLA is required at contribution time. The current contribution
      model is DCO only. A CLA may be introduced in the future only if a
      concrete commercial-relicensing program is contemplated; such a
      future CLA would be a separate instrument and is not part of this
      License.


